<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:ext="clr-namespace:;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:task="clr-namespace:UclOpenCoenDomeNavigationTask;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:core="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:zap="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices.Zapit;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:aud="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Audio;assembly=OpenRigs.Audio"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:dsp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Dsp;assembly=Bonsai.Dsp"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml, read by ReadLabRig, which publishes it to every device piece; the launch's own, which rig-control always sets to C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs. ExperimentRecords and LiveView are not mapped from here: each reads that root as its own ConfigRoot, as a mapping edge into LiveView's StreamDevices would build it before the devices it streams." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
        <Description>This machine's rig.yml (ConfigRoot\MACHINE\rig.yml) read once into the lab rig model: RigConfigs, RigFile, RigConfigDirectory and ConfigRoot, which every device piece reads. First, before anything that reads them.</Description>
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" Description="The mouse's lab ID; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
        <Property Name="SessionId" Description="The session number; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
        <Property Name="LaunchId" Description="The launcher's run id; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
        <Property Name="TaskPath" Description="The task file: rig-control's copy of the one chosen at launch, read at Start for the background noise and again at Go with the form's edits; from the editor, config\task-abstract-av-corridor.yml." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl) over TCP 5561: SubjectId (the mouse's lab ID, or test), SessionId and LaunchId (the launcher's run id, in the manifest) are the launch's; the parameter a controller may change until Go (TrainingStage; the task's own settings are the task file's, which rig-control writes at launch and again at Go with the form's edits, and names in TaskPath); the pieces declare their own parameters and commands (16 Nov 2026). The workflow starts into ready mode (devices connected, spouts homed and at this mouse's positions, live view on, nothing recorded) and reports Ready from Hardware. LaunchSettings (OpenRigs.Control) publishes SubjectId and TaskFilePath (TaskPath) at Start and RunSettings (SubjectId, SessionId) at Go; TrainingStage (OpenRigs.Control) publishes TrainingStage at Go and reports it as the metric trainingStage. SpoutStepSize and the spout commands are DomeHardware's LickSpoutStage's, which takes the step size live and shows its default. RewardLeft and RewardRight each give 2.5 ul before and during a run through the valve's calibration (BehaviorBoard.Rewards includes ManualRewards: Pip's fixed manual drop, 15 Nov 2026).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
              <Property Name="LaunchId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <LaunchId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
                  <Value>0</Value>
                  <Description>Row of the task file's trainingStages to run, 0 to 5 (Tom Childs' stages 1 to 6; a row past the end stops the workflow at Go): suggested from the mouse's earlier experiments.</Description>
                  <Minimum>0</Minimum>
                  <Maximum>5</Maximum>
                  <WholeNumber>true</WholeNumber>
                </Parameter>
              </Parameters>
              <Commands />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="TaskPath" Description="The task file: rig-control's copy of the one chosen at launch, read at Start for the background noise and again at Go with the form's edits; from the editor, config\task-abstract-av-corridor.yml." />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:LaunchSettings.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <TaskPath>..\config\task-abstract-av-corridor.yml</TaskPath>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:TrainingStage.bonsai" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="1" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source2" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskFile</Name>
        <Description>Reads the task file (TaskPath) at Start into LaunchTaskConfig, as rig-control wrote it at launch, for the background noise, which plays from Ready, and src\waveforms\sweep.json into Sweep (LoadSweep), which stops the workflow at Start naming the file when it is missing or naming both rates when its waveforms' rate is not rig.yml's speakerArray.device.sampleRate; at Go, with the form's edits, into TaskConfig, and checks it with the stage, rig.yml and the sweep into TrialRules (CheckTaskAtGo, TrialRules.Create: a stage past the table, a reward zone outside the sweep, the optogenetics rules, the Zapit conditions file). BackgroundNoise stops the workflow at Go if backgroundNoise was changed after launch, as the noise already plays at the launch's level. A real mouse on a rig without hardware triggering is the Zapit group's refusal.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskFilePath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ReadTextFile" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="task:DeserializeFromYaml">
              <task:Type xsi:type="TypeMapping" TypeArguments="task:UclOpenCoenDomeNavigationTaskLogic" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskFilePath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ReadTextFile" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="task:DeserializeFromYaml">
              <task:Type xsi:type="TypeMapping" TypeArguments="task:UclOpenCoenDomeNavigationTaskLogic" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>LaunchTaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SpeakerArray.Device.SampleRate</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:LoadSweep">
                <ext:SweepFile>waveforms\sweep.json</ext:SweepFile>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>Sweep</Name>
              <Description>sweep.json, read at Start (LoadSweep): the sweep the tone files were made for and the rate every waveform was made at, which must be rig.yml's speakerArray.device.sampleRate. The pips' reader takes its rate and pip length from it; CheckTaskAtGo its sweep.</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Sweep</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CheckTaskAtGo" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="20" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="20" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="18" To="20" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source4" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Declarations</Name>
        <Description>Subjects several groups share: the trial loop's events (TrialEvents), the current trial (Trial), trial rows (TrialRow) and stimulus rows (StimulusRows). Zapit's commands and replies are ConnectZapit's, reward requests Rewards'.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="dev:TrialEvent(ext:Trial,ext:StimulusFrame,ext:TrialOutcome)">
              <rx:Name>TrialEvents</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(ext:TrialRow)">
              <rx:Name>TrialRow</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(ext:StimulusStateRow)">
              <rx:Name>StimulusRows</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="ext:Trial">
              <rx:Name>Trial</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogLabExperiment.bonsai">
        <Description>The experiment folder at Go (PathPrefix), BonsaiData_Async, Settings_Rig, Settings_Experiment and the Recording phase. Before Hardware: every device's log waits for PathPrefix, so its definition must read nothing the devices define.</Description>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="DisplayDevice" Description="The display the dome projector is on (DomeHardware's ProjectorDisplay); a launch property." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The dome's devices (OpenRigs.Devices DomeHardware: every device as a piece, each logging itself; the cameras triggered once all three acquire; the speakers and their mixer; the projector, DisplayDevice a launch property), with Ready once the Harp clock is set, the spouts are homed, each camera has sent a frame and the mixer has started, and a stop naming what never came after 180 s.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:DomeHardware.bonsai">
              <Description>Every dome device as a piece, named as in the data (lib-open-rigs Building Blocks): the Ready gate, the timestamp generator's clock, the Behavior board with its reward lines, Zapit line and wheel, both Lickety Splits, the lick spout stage, the three cameras, which start triggering once all three acquire, the speakers (SpeakerMixer) and the projector (ProjectorDisplay, stimuli on DrawStimuli).</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="DisplayDevice" />
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="0" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Display</Name>
        <Description>The grating (BonVision DrawGratings) on the dome: each pip sets its spatial frequency and opacity (TaskLogic); off between trials.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>DrawStimuli</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Double">
              <rx:Name>GratingSpatialFrequency</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="SpatialFrequency" Selector="it" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Double">
              <rx:Name>GratingOpacity</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="Opacity" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawGratings.bonsai">
              <LocationX>0</LocationX>
              <LocationY>30</LocationY>
              <Layer>1</Layer>
              <ExtentX>270</ExtentX>
              <ExtentY>105</ExtentY>
              <SpatialFrequency>0.3</SpatialFrequency>
              <TemporalFrequency>0</TemporalFrequency>
              <Phase>16.8036766</Phase>
              <Angle>90</Angle>
              <SquareWave>false</SquareWave>
              <Contrast>1</Contrast>
              <DutyCycle xsi:nil="true" />
              <Radius>1000</Radius>
              <Aperture>0</Aperture>
              <Opacity>0</Opacity>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source3" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Audio</Name>
        <Description>The dome's sounds, played by DomeHardware's speakers and mixer (OpenRigs.Audio SpeakerMixer: Speakers, rig.yml's speakers and filters loaded once at Start, and the mixer started no sooner than 3 s after Start, as a fault while the sound card boots can blue-screen the PC). At Go, each sound is laid out at the task file's level in dBFS RMS (levelDbfs), which stops the workflow if any would peak at -1 dBFS after equalisation: the pips (PipBuffers, tonePips.levelDbfs; read at Start at sweep.json's rate, one 50 ms pip a buffer, both from Sweep) and the reward tone (RewardTone, rewardTone.levelDbfs) on every rig.yml speaker, each equalised with its filter; the lab's penalty sound is OpenRigs.Audio's PlayPenaltySound, in TaskLogic. The background noise is the BackgroundNoise include's, after this group. TaskLogic sends the pips, the reward tone and the penalty sound to the mixer (StimulusSounds, RewardToneSounds, PenaltySounds), which plays them over each other.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.TonePips.LevelDbfs</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Speakers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Sweep</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="SampleRate" Selector="SampleRate" />
                <Property Name="BufferLength" Selector="PipSamples" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dsp:MatrixReader">
                <dsp:Path>./waveforms/all_waveforms.bin</dsp:Path>
                <dsp:Offset>0</dsp:Offset>
                <dsp:SampleRate>48000</dsp:SampleRate>
                <dsp:ChannelCount>1</dsp:ChannelCount>
                <dsp:BufferLength>2400</dsp:BufferLength>
                <dsp:Depth>F32</dsp:Depth>
                <dsp:Layout>RowMajor</dsp:Layout>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:ToList" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="LevelDbfs" Selector="Item1" />
              </PropertyMappings>
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="aud:SpeakerBuffer">
                <aud:LevelDbfs>-30</aud:LevelDbfs>
                <aud:Equalise>true</aud:Equalise>
                <aud:SyncCopy>true</aud:SyncCopy>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>PipBuffers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.RewardTone.LevelDbfs</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Speakers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dsp:MatrixReader">
                <dsp:Path>./waveforms/reward_tone.bin</dsp:Path>
                <dsp:Offset>0</dsp:Offset>
                <dsp:SampleRate>0</dsp:SampleRate>
                <dsp:ChannelCount>1</dsp:ChannelCount>
                <dsp:BufferLength>0</dsp:BufferLength>
                <dsp:Depth>F32</dsp:Depth>
                <dsp:Layout>RowMajor</dsp:Layout>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="LevelDbfs" Selector="Item1" />
              </PropertyMappings>
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="aud:SpeakerBuffer">
                <aud:LevelDbfs>-36</aud:LevelDbfs>
                <aud:Equalise>true</aud:Equalise>
                <aud:SyncCopy>false</aud:SyncCopy>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RewardToneBuffer</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="1" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="13" To="18" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Audio:BackgroundNoise.bonsai">
        <Description>The background noise, the lab's one file, rig.yml's speakerArray.backgroundNoise (60 s of white noise, 32-bit float), unequalised on every speaker at the launched task file's backgroundNoise.levelDbfs from Ready; Go stops if the task file changed backgroundNoise after launch.</Description>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:Zapit.ConnectForTask.bonsai" />
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Logging</Name>
        <Description>Everything else written to the experiment folder (LogLabExperiment, before Hardware, makes the folder): TaskLogs (OpenRigs.Logging) writes Settings_Task (the task file as JSON), BonsaiData_Trial and Zapit's logs, ExperimentLogs the task's own BonsaiData_StimulusState; each device logs itself; Rewards (its DeliverReward) logs each reward and each calibrated valve's file; ExperimentRecords, last but LiveView, takes the controller's events, records the Harp devices and writes the manifest.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>ExperimentLogs</Name>
              <Description>The task's own log that waits for the experiment folder (PathPrefix): BonsaiData_StimulusState (LogData of StimulusRows).</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>StimulusRows</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogData.bonsai">
                    <LogName>BonsaiData_StimulusState</LogName>
                    <Selector />
                    <AutoFlush>true</AutoFlush>
                    <Extension>csv</Extension>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="task:SerializeToJson">
                <task:Formatting>Indented</task:Formatting>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:TaskLogs.bonsai" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Status</Name>
        <Description>The current trial's facts as metrics, named as BonsaiData_Trial's columns (trialNumber, rewardSizeUl, laserCondition; the trainingStage is TrainingStage's), at each trial's start; rig-control computes counts and performance from the trial rows.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Trial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>trialNumber</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>trialNumber</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>rewardSizeUl</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>rewardSizeUl</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>laserCondition</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>laserCondition</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.Rewards.bonsai" />
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskLogic</Name>
        <Description>The task in tested C# (src\Extensions\TrialLogic.cs, tests\Extensions.Tests) on lib-open-rigs' TrialLoop: once the experiment folder exists and the tones are loaded, TrialRules comes on the next Harp clock tick (OnNextTick); RunTrials draws each trial (TrialDraw) at the start of its interval (the last outcome after any timeout), has a hardware-triggered Zapit armed during it (Arm, once the last trigger line has fallen), starts it (Start, beep 0: the interval's end less the lead, max(laserToStimulusSeconds, 0), or later until the stage's quiet waits hold, the left spout's alone), then runs it along the virtual track (VirtualTrack) with a pip every 50 ms from the lead after the trial start, all on the Harp clock (Timestamp), until the outcome. Its events (TrialEvents, each kind picked by PickTrialEvents) drive the hardware here: Start publishes the trial (Trial); Arm sends Zapit the trial's condition (laser-off trials at 0 mW); Trigger, laserToStimulusSeconds before the first pip (after it if negative), in an optogenetics experiment only, raises the ZapitTrigger line (BehaviorBoard.SetZapitTriggerLine) (and on a software-triggered rig sends the StartStimulus), and RunTrials stops the task if Zapit has not answered by then; each Update (a pip) plays the pip and sets the grating; Outcome writes the trial row, rewards (RewardRequests, left spout) or plays the penalty sound (PlayPenaltySound); TriggerOff clears the trigger line triggerHoldSeconds after the outcome. Zapit adds no time.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Value</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>WheelDistanceCm</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LickStateLeft</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ZapitReplies</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:RunTrials" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>Optogenetics?</Name>
              <Description>An optogenetics experiment: the rules have a laser (optogenetics.useZapit).</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Laser != null</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>Zapit</Name>
              <Description>Once at Go, in an optogenetics experiment (the rules have a laser), so a task without Zapit needs no rig.yml zapit block: each trial's StartStimulus (ArmZapit: its condition, laser on with the task's power or off at 0 mW, continuous until StopZapit; at Arm on a hardware-triggered rig, else at the Trigger) and the laser's stop (LaserOnUntilOutcome).</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                      <dev:Kind>Arm</dev:Kind>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Trial</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                      <dev:Kind>Trigger</dev:Kind>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Trial</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="HardwareTriggered" Selector="Zapit.HardwareTriggered" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Name>ArmZapit</Name>
                    <Description>The trial's StartStimulus (lib-open-rigs' ZapitTrialCommand: its condition, laser on with the task's power or off at 0 mW, continuous until StopZapit). On a hardware-triggered rig (rig.yml's zapit.hardwareTriggered) sent at the trial's Arm event, during the interval; without, Zapit starts the laser on receipt, so it is sent at the trigger.</Description>
                    <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitTrialCommand">
                      <zap:HardwareTriggered>false</zap:HardwareTriggered>
                      <zap:DurationSeconds>0</zap:DurationSeconds>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>ZapitCommands</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
                    <Name>LaserOnUntilOutcome</Name>
                    <Description>From the trigger, stops Zapit once per optogenetics trial: at the outcome, at laserMaxSeconds on the Harp clock (LaserCap), or at laserMaxSeconds on the wall clock (LaserBackstop), should the board stall (the one wall-clock wait in TaskLogic). A trial that ends before its trigger has no laser; the next StartStimulus disarms it.</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                            <dev:Kind>Outcome</dev:Kind>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                            <dev:Kind>LaserCap</dev:Kind>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Name>LaserMax</scr:Name>
                          <scr:Expression>TimeSpan.FromSeconds(Trial.laserMaxSeconds)</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="DueTime" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Name>LaserBackstop</Name>
                          <Description>Stops Zapit laserMaxSeconds after the trigger on the computer's clock, should the Harp board stall so that LaserCap never comes: the one wall-clock wait in TaskLogic. It logs nothing itself; whichever of the three comes first stops the laser.</Description>
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Timer">
                            <rx:DueTime>PT12.5S</rx:DueTime>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                            <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="zap:StopZapit" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>ZapitCommands</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                        <Expression xsi:type="Unit" />
                        <Expression xsi:type="Unit" />
                        <Expression xsi:type="Unit" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="4" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="7" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="13" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="14" To="8" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="15" To="8" Label="Source3" />
                        <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="9" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                <dev:Kind>Start</dev:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>Trial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
              <Set>true</Set>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                <dev:Kind>Update</dev:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PipBuffers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:PipBuffer" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>StimulusSounds</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Update.Row.visualSpatialFrequencyCpd</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>GratingSpatialFrequency</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Update.GratingOpacity</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>GratingOpacity</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CreateStimulusRow" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>StimulusRows</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                <dev:Kind>Outcome</dev:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="DoubleProperty">
                <Value>0</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>GratingOpacity</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CreateTrialRow" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TrialRow</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>Rewarded?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Outcome.Rewarded</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Outcome.Reward</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>RewardRequests</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RewardToneBuffer</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>RewardToneSounds</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>PenaltySound?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Outcome.PenaltySound</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Audio:PlayPenaltySound.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                <dev:Kind>TriggerOff</dev:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
              <Set>false</Set>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                <dev:Kind>Trigger</dev:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PickTrialEvents">
                <dev:Kind>Start</dev:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial.rngSeed</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogRngSeed.bonsai">
              <Description>The seed every draw of the experiment follows from (the task file's rngSeed, or one drawn at Go when it is null), logged once at trial 1's start.</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PipBuffers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item1</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>OnNextTick</Name>
              <Description>The rules, once the experiment folder exists and the tones are loaded, stamped with the next Harp clock tick and given from the clock's thread (lib-open-rigs' OpenRigs.Core OnNextTick), with no lock held, so trial 1 runs as every later one does.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:OnNextTick" />
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="5" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source4" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source5" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="46" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="18" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="23" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="23" To="24" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="27" To="28" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="28" To="29" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="28" To="31" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="31" To="32" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="28" To="33" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="33" To="34" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="34" To="35" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="33" To="37" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="36" To="37" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="37" To="38" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="38" To="39" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="28" To="40" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="42" To="43" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="43" To="44" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="45" To="46" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="47" To="48" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="48" To="49" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="40" To="41" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="49" To="50" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="51" To="54" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="52" To="54" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="53" To="54" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="54" To="55" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="55" To="56" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="56" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="56" To="0" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:ExperimentRecords.bonsai">
        <Description>The controller's events (LogControlEvents), every Harp device in rig.yml checked at Start and recorded (RecordHarpDevices: the Behavior board, the timestamp generator, both stepper drivers and both Lickety Splits), and manifest.json (ExperimentManifest: rig.yml and every file it names and this mouse's spout positions by hash ({RigFiles}), schemas\trial-columns.yml, and what the experiment must leave: a folder for each device in rig.yml, the Harp device records, the three settings files and BonsaiData (Trial, Async and StimulusState), Zapit's logs in an optogenetics experiment). Last but LiveView, as it finds each device by the subjects published before it.</Description>
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
        <IngestScript>coen-dome-navigation</IngestScript>
        <ExpectedFiles>auto;harp;Settings/Settings_Rig_;Settings/Settings_Task_;Settings/Settings_Experiment_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_Trial_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_Async_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_StimulusState_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_ZapitReplies_?Optogenetics;Settings/Settings_ZapitConditions_?Optogenetics</ExpectedFiles>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every device in this machine's rig.yml that the workflow publishes, over ZeroMQ, for the live view (OpenRigs.LiveView): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558, from Start, in ready mode too. The three cameras as Camera-Face/Pupil/Body.video, 5 JPEG frames a second at 320 x 240, and the Behavior board's encoder from BehaviorBoard-Main.Data, 10 a second; each rate and size can be changed in rig.yml under the device's liveView:. Also elapsed, seconds since the experiment folder appeared, and liveview, this workflow and its commit. Every message carries the rig and the session key, ready until the experiment folder exists. Last in the workflow, because it streams only subjects built before it. A port already in use stops the workflow at Start.</Description>
        <lv:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</lv:ConfigRoot>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
